Z||000005||Standard||04-27-2000||02:35 AM||||whoooo boy, what a day...  started out great.  Put it my pioneer 2-way 4x6's, they sound great, even with the stock stereo.  much clearer sound now. Also have pioneer 2-way 4x10's up front.. just need a deck.  Ran some errands, then washed the car.  decided to fiddle around with some things after that, my left turn signal hasn't blinked since I got the car, just gave my that steady green arrow.. turns out that the weatherpack for the connector in the front turn signal was pulled out a little bit, not allowing the contacts to hit the bulb fully.  like Patrick said.. sometimes it's the simplest things.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I was feeling pretty good, so I decided to drive down to fleet farm and spend some money.. killed an Acura legend V6(of course the only mod on it was some nice looking 17" or 18" a-r twisted tuner wheels.. it wasn't covered with stickers and had stock exhaust tips.. kinda only half-rice) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> multiple times.  goes downhill from there... the acura had turned off and I was sitting at a stop light.  light turns green, i start driving.  Then I feel the GT take a little weave to the left..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> my first thought was "oh great, there goes a tire.." so I take it easy into a parking lot and do the inspection.. well, the tires were fine.  Then I kick each of the wheels.. and there it is, drivers side front wheel.  "oh guano.. not the ball joint!"  Jack it up, and yep, that upper ball joint is ready to go.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> after a few more muttered "guano's" I lower it down and take it easy back home.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||04-27-2000||02:36 AM||||Well, just about home.. I'm on the offramp waiting for the light to turn so I can make a left and get home.  Light turns green, I put out into the intersection.. and all of a sudden this green bonneville flys straight by me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> if I was 3 feet farther out my front end would have been knocked back onto the freeway!  I lay on my horn.. the light up ahead is red, and he actually stopped for this one.  I pulled up next to him, and just glared at him.. my mind was going to fast to think of anything else to do.. he just kinda looks over like he didn't do a damn thing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> after that the night got a little less exciting.. adjusted my headlights.. popped my decklid open and saw just how much my plug wires are arcing.. wow.  what a light show! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> just put in new wires about a month ago.. borg warner 7mm.. guess I'll go with the accels next time.  anyways.. I think that's the end of my story.  hope I can find someplace with ubj's in stock.. at least I have tomorrow off.  if you made it this far, congrats!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I had to cut this into two pieces.. wouldn't let me send it all in one message.. guess I'm just long-winded today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||5
